# The build context is the source and the packs, nothing else.
#
# The two big ones are not optional: DarkRPG/ is the ~3.6 GB save and build/cache/ is the payload
# cache (hundreds of thousands of small files). Docker tars the context before the first instruction
# runs, so including either means a multi-minute upload on every build, for a server that is told at
# runtime where the save actually is.

# --- the world: input data, mounted at run time ---
DarkRPG/

# --- derived, per-machine, huge ---
build/cache/
build/cache-test/
build/assets-test/
build/ov_backup/
build/shells_v2_backup/
build/rescue/
build/ledger/actions.bin

# --- version control: 2.8 GB of history the image never reads ---
.git/
.gitignore

# --- local scratch: probes, screenshots, one-off scripts ---
build/*.png
build/*.jpg
build/*.txt
build/*.log
build/*.json
build/*.md
build/*.js
build/*.mjs
build/*.cjs
build/*.sh
build/*.ps1
build/*.py
build/scratch/
build/tmp/
logs/
deploy/
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
